<title>USA: Texaco U.S. Gulf operations back to normal.</title>
<headline>Texaco U.S. Gulf operations back to normal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Corp said its U.S. Gulf operations were back to normal after evacuating employees from production platforms there ahead of Hurricane Danny last week.</p>
<p>The company began returning the 365 workers to platforms Friday after pulling them out Thursday. The company produces about 40,000 barrels per day of oil and about 200 million cubic feet of natural gas in the region.</p>
<p>&quot;Everything's back to normal,&quot; said Pierre De Gruy, Texaco spokesman in New Orleans.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
